// Feed rendering and row measurement.
//
// Entries are laid out in a single scrolling column inside the viewport. Each
// entry's real pixel height depends on how much text it carries and whether it
// shows an attachment strip, so heights vary from row to row and are only known
// once a row has been laid out. As rows render, their measured heights are fed
// back to the virtualizer so its offset table reflects real geometry rather
// than the initial estimate.
//
// A pinned footer band ("you're all caught up") sits below the entries and is
// always kept visible at the bottom of the shell; the scroll column reserves a
// matching region beneath the last entry so the entries can scroll clear of it.
//
// The band has a soft lead-in ribbon carrying the per-channel "while you were
// away" digest and, below it, the solid bar. Both are measured here so the
// caller can decide how the scroll column reserves space beneath the last
// entry and how far a jumped-to entry has to travel.

